From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a launcher's own client library keeps its imports.

Proton runs Windows games against a launcher's Linux client: ntdll loads
lsteamclient.dll in place of the launcher's client library and points its
tier0_s64 and vstdlib_s64 imports at ntdll. On the console there is no
Linux client and no lsteamclient.dll, and the launcher's client itself
is a Windows program here. Its client library got stubs for its
tier0 and vstdlib functions, its DllMain returned 0, and the launcher
loaded it twenty times before "InternalAPI_Init_Internal failed, most
likely because you are missing a 32-bit dependency" and the "problem
with your installation" box (2026-10-05, with +module; record removed from the tree; in git history). The
bridge is off unless PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=0.
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -1156,9 +1156,14 @@
 
     if (use != -1) return use;
 
-    use = !get_env( L"PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT", env, sizeof(env) ) || *env == '0';
+    /* PS5: no launcher's Linux client runs beside the console for lsteamclient to bridge to,
+     * and lsteamclient.dll is not built. The launcher's own client library runs instead, and
+     * it needs its own tier0 and vstdlib: pointed at ntdll, their functions were stubs
+     * and its DllMain failed ("missing a 32-bit dependency" of its client library).
+     * PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=0 turns the bridge back on. */
+    use = get_env( L"PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT", env, sizeof(env) ) && *env == '0';
     if (!use)
-        ERR("lsteamclient disabled.\n");
+        TRACE("lsteamclient disabled.\n");
     return use;
 }
 
